# main carries the whole vault: every plugin, snippet and theme.
#
# .gitignore is itself a tracked file, so each branch carries its own copy and
# git switches these rules for you on checkout. The other branches narrow this:
#
#   feature/<plugin>   adds a `scope-branch` block that ignores every plugin
#                      except the ones under development, plus the vault's own
#                      content folders. Set it with .githooks/scope-branch.
#   data/<project>     removes the /data/ line below, which is what makes a
#                      project's notes trackable there.
#
# See "Version control" in .obsidian/plugins/schema-sync/README.md.
# .githooks/pre-push is the safety net. Enable it once per clone:
#
#     git config core.hooksPath .githooks

# Vault data lives on data/<name> branches only.
/data/

# A nested duplicate of the vault, left over from an earlier layout.
/MyVault/
